{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20489",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.21,
      "end_seconds": 4.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Sorry I'm a a little late, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.55,
      "end_seconds": 10.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.46,
      "end_seconds": 17.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "I've been dealing with a burn on my left forearm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.23,
      "end_seconds": 19.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "When did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.07,
      "end_seconds": 34.27,
      "duration_seconds": 13.2,
      "text": "it's been going on for about two weeks. My neighbour said I should get it looked at. Oh, and a blister. That's been about the same, about a week"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.57,
      "end_seconds": 49.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "okay, what about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.55,
      "end_seconds": 53.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "My father has Parkinson's disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.78,
      "end_seconds": 58.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.56,
      "end_seconds": 70.37,
      "duration_seconds": 10.81,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years. I swim twice a week. Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.28,
      "end_seconds": 82.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.97,
      "end_seconds": 86.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Nothing, I haven't had any operations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.67,
      "end_seconds": 93.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "So, do you have any medical conditions I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.44,
      "end_seconds": 97.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "not really, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.11,
      "end_seconds": 101.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.56,
      "end_seconds": 106.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Not to my knowledge, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.87,
      "end_seconds": 109.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Do you take any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.04,
      "end_seconds": 113.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "No, nothing at the moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.9,
      "end_seconds": 135.52,
      "duration_seconds": 7.62,
      "text": "let me check a few things. Any trouble breathing, fever, pus or burn on the face?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.69,
      "end_seconds": 138.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.81,
      "end_seconds": 143.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.33,
      "end_seconds": 147.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.99,
      "end_seconds": 153.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "Can I check a a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.6,
      "end_seconds": 169.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.78,
      "end_seconds": 191.24,
      "duration_seconds": 9.46,
      "text": "Okay: saturation 99 percent, temperature is 36.8 degrees, respiratory rate 14, BP is 120 over 79, pulse is 75 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.33,
      "end_seconds": 194.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.15,
      "end_seconds": 199.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Don't worry, we'll discuss it in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.2,
      "end_seconds": 205.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.75,
      "end_seconds": 208.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "raise your arm for me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.08,
      "end_seconds": 236.04,
      "duration_seconds": 8.96,
      "text": "there is a five-centimetre area of redness with an intact blister on the left forearm, and it blanches and is painful"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.23,
      "end_seconds": 251.62,
      "duration_seconds": 11.39,
      "text": "good, you can sit up again from what you've told me and what I found, I think we're dealing with a superficial partial-thickness burn at this stage"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.86,
      "end_seconds": 291.22,
      "duration_seconds": 26.36,
      "text": "For this, paracetamol, 1 gram, every six hours if needed, for three days. That's for burn pain. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Cool the area under running water for twenty minutes and cover it with a non-stick dressing, and leave the blister alone. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.03,
      "end_seconds": 313.4,
      "duration_seconds": 21.37,
      "text": "keep an eye out, and if the burn becomes smelly, spreads or you get a fever, call us the same day or go to emergency i'd like you back in three days can you tell me the plan back in your own words, so I know I've explained it clearly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 315.06,
      "end_seconds": 325.77,
      "duration_seconds": 10.71,
      "text": "so, I take the paracetamol, 1 gram, every six hours if needed and come back in three days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.69,
      "end_seconds": 331.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "yes, exactly right. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 333.21,
      "end_seconds": 336.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "no, that's all thanks a lot"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.59,
      "end_seconds": 338.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}